60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option C is a fantasy of precision that would cost us a small fortune to implement. Option A, while simple, is a silent agreement to let those in the colder rooms suffer in silence. I find it quite bleak.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I agree that Option C is way too expensive! But Option A is actually the only one that doesn't sound like a total nightmare for the person doing the math. It's just one simple division!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option A is indeed simple, but I worry it may be too simple. If we ignore the disparities in usage and the history of friction, we might only be delaying the next disagreement.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option A is too volatile. With the swings I saw in the statements, a flat share means our monthly costs will be unpredictable, which is a significant financial stress. Option B offers the stability we need.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think Option A might make people grumpy again if the bills change a lot. Option B sounds a bit more peaceful because we know what to expect, and we can talk about it together at the end.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, @Minato, you make a compelling case for stability. Option B prevents the monthly financial whiplash of Option A, though it doesn't explicitly solve the ""refrigerator room"" dilemma. Still, it is far more rational than paying for meters.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Victoria, @Minato, I see why you like Option B, but wait! Settling the difference at the end of the year sounds like a huge project! Who's going to spend their whole evening doing all that math? It's just delaying the headache!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, while a year-end settlement requires effort, it is a small price to pay for stability. I believe a predictable monthly cost would prevent the late payments and confusion I discovered in our history.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, the effort of a single annual calculation is far preferable to the monthly anxiety of unpredictable bills. Stability allows us to budget properly, which is the only way to ensure no one is unfairly burdened by a sudden spike.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Mio, I understand it sounds like a lot of work, but maybe we can all help each other do the math together? If we do it as a group, it won't be a headache and we can be honest about everything.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minato, a group math session sounds like a delightful way to spend an evening, provided we don't end up arguing over decimals. Option B is the most elegant compromise; it provides stability and avoids the absurdity of Option C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Minato, that's a sweet idea, but group math usually just means one person does the work while everyone else watches! I'm still worried, but if everyone really helps, maybe Option B is okay. It's definitely better than Option C!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I believe we have found a path toward harmony. Option B addresses the volatility that causes stress and the unpredictability that led to past delays. It is a gentle way to ensure stability for everyone.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, I believe the trade-off is worth it. The mental burden of a single annual settlement is negligible compared to the monthly fear of a bill that feels like a second rent. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I agree with Victoria. I think Option B is the best because it keeps things calm every month. If we do the final part together, we can make sure everyone feels heard and happy. I vote for Option B!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems the consensus has shifted toward stability. While Option B doesn't magically warm the colder rooms, it prevents the financial chaos of Option A. I shall vote for Option B. Logic and peace prevail.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm still a little nervous about that year-end math, but you guys have convinced me! If we really do it together and keep it simple, it'll be fine. I vote for Option B!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. Option B provides the predictability we need to avoid the friction of the past. It is a thoughtful compromise that preserves our collective peace of mind. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I have already cast my vote for Option B. It is the only choice that provides the financial predictability necessary to manage our budget without the prohibitive cost of installation. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm so happy we all agree! Let's promise to be really kind to each other when we do the final settling. I'm voting for Option B too!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
